{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations","id":898955,"title":"Alternate Origin for Abyssal Exaltations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-25T08:36:41-07:00","id":898955,"title":"Alternate Origin for Abyssal Exaltations","content":"I had an epiphany this morning when someone brought up the &quot;Abyssals and Solars are two sides of the same coin&quot; metaphor. What if, instead of Abyssals being corrupted Solars, Abyssal origins instead are a result of the Usurpation, the sorcerous working the Sidereals used to imprison the Solar Exaltations, and the first mass murder of the Solars. Essentially, the Abyssal Exaltations are grave goods copies of Solar Exaltations. The Abyssal Exaltations were imprisoned in the same way that the Solars were until, by sympathetic response, the Solars returned, which explains the only recent emergence of the Abyssals.<br /> <br /> What sort of implications would this have for the Abyssal condition? What changes in themes would you expect? Would any traditionally Abyssal feature no longer make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:54:47-07:00","id":898971,"title":"","content":"I think this is cool. I won't say it should be canon, but it might be a really neat way of making Abyssal Exaltations into something that don't need to be &quot;redeemed&quot;.<br /> <br /> Especially if the &quot;offer&quot; of the Black Exaltation isn't &quot;agree to serve Oblivion and murder the world!&quot; but rather &quot;agree to serve the Underworld&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-25-2016, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:32:19-07:00","id":899006,"title":"","content":"Interesting. If the exaltation is considered grave goods, does that mean it disintegrates when it enters Creation like all other grave goods unless sheltered by a host? If so, how would anyone ever exalt as one? Only canny daring mortals who venture into the Underworld are worthy of Abyssal exaltation? I could see this origin being a stronger reason why Abyssals can't respire essence in Creation than 1E and 2E gave us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:34:06-07:00","id":899014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899006#post899006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. If the exaltation is considered grave goods, does that mean it disintegrates when it enters Creation like all other grave goods unless sheltered by a host? If so, how would anyone ever exalt as one? Only canny daring mortals who venture into the Underworld are worthy of Abyssal exaltation? I could see this origin being a stronger reason why Abyssals can't respire essence in Creation than 1E and 2E gave us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget shadowlands. In my first 1E game, it was theorized (by the players) that Abyssals were Solars who Exalted in a shadowland, thus absorbing some of the deathly Essence of the Underworld. Grave goods Exaltations could potentially find hosts in shadowlands, even if only at night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:39:05-07:00","id":899023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899006#post899006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. If the exaltation is considered grave goods, does that mean it disintegrates when it enters Creation like all other grave goods unless sheltered by a host? If so, how would anyone ever exalt as one?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably go with either &quot;Exaltations are special&quot; or &quot;The Exaltation crosses over from the Underworld at the moment of death&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:41:18-07:00","id":899024,"title":"","content":"Don't know how I feel about Abyssal Exaltations just coming into existence, but I'd much prefer mirroring and opposing an extant Solar to them being stolen and corrupted Solars. Personally, the Exigence gave me hope for a more compelling origin for Death's/Hell's Lawgivers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:41:50-07:00","id":899025,"title":"","content":"I like this idea so much better than &quot;the Deathlords knocked over Chejop Kejak's super secret safe and ran off with some Exaltations.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:55:28-07:00","id":899044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899025#post899025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this idea so much better than &quot;the Deathlords knocked over Chejop Kejak's super secret safe and ran off with some Exaltations.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps they, or the Neverborn, were trying to create their own with a Void Circle working and ended up breaking the Jade prison and getting Abyssals instead. There might be some degree of limitation that this imposes, perhaps the number of Abyssals cannot be greater than the number of Solars or an Abyssal can only be Exalted if the corresponding Solar is, something having to do with light casting shadow perhaps.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting if there was a resonance (hah!) of some kind between an Abyssal and their Solar &quot;original&quot; which could perhaps become analogous to the Lunar bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:56:15-07:00","id":899045,"title":"","content":"I love Abyssals as &quot;grave goods&quot; Exaltations!<br /> <br /> A while back, I banged out a bunch of &quot;Lore 0 Exalted&quot; takes on the setting (which is to say, Creation looks the same to the casual observer, but the secret histories and behind-the-scenes power-players are all different), and this was one explanation for the Abyssals - I think it's pretty great. Especially due to the implications of a Solar meeting the Abyssal version of her own incarnations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:58:05-07:00","id":899049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899044#post899044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps they, or the Neverborn, were trying to create their own with a Void Circle working and ended up breaking the Jade prison and getting Abyssals instead. There might be some degree of limitation that this imposes, perhaps the number of Abyssals cannot be greater than the number of Solars or an Abyssal can only be Exalted if the corresponding Solar is, something having to do with light casting shadow perhaps.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting if there was a resonance (hah!) of some kind between an Abyssal and their Solar &quot;original&quot; which could perhaps become analogous to the Lunar bond.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the idea of each Solar having an Abyssal foil. I considered having a character with his first age self being a Deathlord. Once I saw the Deathlord stats, that seemed to be a little too extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:35:11-07:00","id":899194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899024#post899024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know how I feel about Abyssal Exaltations just coming into existence</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rule it a one time accidental never to be repeated event.<br /> <br /> How would the deathlords react to these Abyssal Exalted? Suddenly there are Solar power level beings completely comfortable in the Underworld. Recruitment? Patronage? Destruction? I suppose it would depend on the deathlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:41:55-07:00","id":899205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899194#post899194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the deathlords react to these Abyssal Exalted? Suddenly there are Solar power level beings completely comfortable in the Underworld. Recruitment? Patronage? Destruction? I suppose it would depend on the deathlord.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like Abyssals having a variety of ways to relate to Deathlords besides &quot;lord/knight&quot;. It would definitely expand what an Abyssal game could be about. Are you fighting to free ghosts from a Deathlord's soulsteel fist? Are you a necrotech crafter, selling his services to a Deathlord? You a ronin knight, traveling from shadowland to shadowland, protecting ancestor worship? <br /> <br /> Though I suppose that may step on some Solar themes. I'm not sure if Abyssals should be &quot;Solars, except doing Solar shit in the underworld!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:44:41-07:00","id":899209,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this is a Little Sidejacking.... But going off of this Idea... The Green Sun Princes/Infernals &quot;Might&quot; be the Great Curse's Ultimate Goal... A &quot;Copy&quot; of the Solar Exaltation that leeched off of them for so long that they are now something of their own... and It's all part of the Plan for the Dragon....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:51:03-07:00","id":899217,"title":"","content":"Just as an aside, I remember back during early First Edition (before the release of Exalted: the Abyssals) there were quite a few theories on what the Abyssal Exalted were. There was this cool theory i particular that held that the Solars who had been captured and taken into the Imperial Manse were used by the Empress in some sort of magical ritual. When she vanished, the Solar Exaltations (or now Abyssal Exaltations) she had corrupted broke free, thus the origins of the Abyssals. I never used this in a game, but it's still something I look back fondly on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:07:21-07:00","id":899234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899024#post899024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know how I feel about Abyssal Exaltations just coming into existence</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not &quot;just&quot; if it relied on something as crazy as the Sidereals sealing the Solar Exaltations away from the world, and possibly also a bunch of Deathlords accidentally breaking the Jade Prison by trying to create Abyssal Exaltations, or perhaps the Abyssal Exaltations being released in the Underworld when Hell found and cracked open the Jade Prison to capture Solar Exaltations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:19:05-07:00","id":899244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899205#post899205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Abyssals having a variety of ways to relate to Deathlords besides &quot;lord/knight&quot;. It would definitely expand what an Abyssal game could be about. Are you fighting to free ghosts from a Deathlord's soulsteel fist? Are you a necrotech crafter, selling his services to a Deathlord? You a ronin knight, traveling from shadowland to shadowland, protecting ancestor worship? <br /> <br /> Though I suppose that may step on some Solar themes. I'm not sure if Abyssals should be &quot;Solars, except doing Solar shit in the underworld!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? They could do that too! Heck, Solars could also do everything you mentioned above! But yeah, I'm with you, this seems to really open the possibilities for Abyssal stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:28:15-07:00","id":899257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations#post898955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of implications would this have for the Abyssal condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for one thing, it means Sidereals are to blame for their existence. So obviously I love it.<br /> <br /> Really though I'm curious about a few aspects of it, like roughly how many Abyssal Exaltations are there floating about now, 300, one for each Solar? Are these two sets of exalted power linked somehow? Is it possible for these two hypothetical Exalted to know they share an exaltation?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:29:03-07:00","id":899258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899209#post899209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this is a Little Sidejacking.... But going off of this Idea... The Green Sun Princes/Infernals &quot;Might&quot; be the Great Curse's Ultimate Goal... A &quot;Copy&quot; of the Solar Exaltation that leeched off of them for so long that they are now something of their own... and It's all part of the Plan for the Dragon....</div> </div> </div> </div>That would solve one of my two problems with the starting theory of this thread: Where do the Infernals come from?<br /> <br /> My other problem is why was the Jade Prison broken open and by who? The Deathlords don't need to corrupt them and Sidreals don't want them out, so who did it? Now this could be left as a mystery, giving a more mythic feeling to Exalted, but I do think some sort of reason should exist for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:30:23-07:00","id":899261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899258#post899258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would solve one of my two problems with the starting theory of this thread: Where do the Infernals come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't Infernals still be corrupted Solar Exaltations, especially if the prison was broken by the forces of Hell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:48:54-07:00","id":899280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899261#post899261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't Infernals still be corrupted Solar Exaltations, especially if the prison was broken by the forces of Hell?</div> </div> </div> </div>And if it was mortals or lesser demons who located and opened the Jade Prison, then we don't have the &quot;hyper-competent Deathlords screwed up royally&quot; as a problem.<br /> <br /> Would the Abyssal Charm set need to tone down the murder and Oblivion aspects if they are no longer the creations of the Deathlords and the Neverborn? Would their Medicine Charms need to move away from necrotech?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T13:05:36-07:00","id":899305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899261#post899261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't Infernals still be corrupted Solar Exaltations, especially if the prison was broken by the forces of Hell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh i just thought it was an interesting idea.. The Great Curse Left without a Host to Corrupt has warped and Twisted itself into something More.. Something Different.<br /> <br /> They could still be what they are/were Just as an Idea to add to this (It also means we could have a Full Assembly of Abyssals and Infernals, abit of an interesting idea.. 300 of each of the 3 types Well 270 odd by Estimation)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T13:16:04-07:00","id":899315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899280#post899280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Abyssal Charm set need to tone down the murder and Oblivion aspects if they are no longer the creations of the Deathlords and the Neverborn? Would their Medicine Charms need to move away from necrotech?</div> </div> </div> </div>I say mirror the Solar Charmset giving the aesthetics an Abyssal treatment. You may even consider giving them a shadow theme instead of the default gory bloody theme of the Abyssal Exalted. They really would be a shadow version of the Solars. A shadow through the valley of death type shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T13:54:19-07:00","id":899359,"title":"","content":"Mirror charms didn't exactly go over well the last time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:02:19-07:00","id":899367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899315#post899315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say mirror the Solar Charmset giving the aesthetics an Abyssal treatment. You may even consider giving them a shadow theme instead of the default gory bloody theme of the Abyssal Exalted. They really would be a shadow version of the Solars. A shadow through the valley of death type shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they mirror the Solar Exalted by letting Abyssals excel at all of the arts of ghosts rather than the arts of the living.<br /> <br /> A Dusk Caste takes the example of First And Forsaken Lion further than that dread iron ghost can go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:28:56-07:00","id":899400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899261#post899261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't Infernals still be corrupted Solar Exaltations, especially if the prison was broken by the forces of Hell?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a solution is a possibility, but note I was starting that post from the assumption that the Infernals are copies of Solars not corrupted Solar. Yet the situation could be different depending on what is wanted or desired. Some ideas I had thought up of:<br /> <br /> 1) The Scarlet Empress used the Imperial Manse to break the Jade Prison as a fulfilment of a threat against the Sidreals as she feels they are controlling her life too much. I know it's a little contrived, but her disappearance could be explained by her body being vaporized as the Imperial Manse overheated to power the super attack needed to destroy the Jade Prison.<br /> <br /> 2) Birth of a Greater elemental dragon broke the prison in it's initial rampage.<br /> <br /> 3) A surviving Solar sorcerer found the Jade Prison and decided to make it go BOOM!<br /> <br /> 4) There was no Jade Prison under the sea. Instead it is a small box kept by the Unconquered Sun, who has been convinced by Kejop of it's necessity. He keeps this for many years, unaware of Creation's decreasing glory and safety. Only when the prayers of some unknown mortal reached his equivalent of a prayer inbox for a symbolic duty to the leadership of Yu Shan, did the Unconquered Sun once more see fit to release the Solars.<br /> <br /> 5) Rakan Thulio did it. You can always blame Rakan Thulio for it. The Sidreals probably do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:33:05-07:00","id":899402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899400#post899400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a solution is a possibility, but note I was starting that post from the assumption that the Infernals are copies of Solars not corrupted Solar. Yet the situation could be different depending on what is wanted or desired. Some ideas I had thought up of:<br /> <br /> 1) The Scarlet Empress used the Imperial Manse to break the Jade Prison as a fulfilment of a threat against the Sidreals as she feels they are controlling her life too much. I know it's a little contrived, but her disappearance could be explained by her body being vaporized as the Imperial Manse overheated to power the super attack needed to destroy the Jade Prison.<br /> <br /> 2) Birth of a Greater elemental dragon broke the prison in it's initial rampage.<br /> <br /> 3) A surviving Solar sorcerer found the Jade Prison and decided to make it go BOOM!<br /> <br /> 4) There was no Jade Prison under the sea. Instead it is a small box kept by the Unconquered Sun, who has been convinced by Kejop of it's necessity. He keeps this for many years, unaware of Creation's decreasing glory and safety. Only when the prayers of some unknown mortal reached his equivalent of a prayer inbox for a symbolic duty to the leadership of Yu Shan, did the Unconquered Sun once more see fit to release the Solars.<br /> <br /> 5) Rakan Thulio did it. You can always blame Rakan Thulio for it. The Sidreals probably do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 6) The Sidereals did it, or rather the Gold Faction did it. Since Sidereals are the ones that imprisoned the Solars the first time around, it is Sidereals who must free them once more, so a rogue band of Gold Stars open (not destroy) the Jade Prison, risking censure and potentially execution to &quot;save the world.&quot; And yet, the Jade Prison still exists, open but not destroyed. What uses might it find in the future?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T15:00:22-07:00","id":899436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899209#post899209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this is a Little Sidejacking.... But going off of this Idea... The Green Sun Princes/Infernals &quot;Might&quot; be the Great Curse's Ultimate Goal... A &quot;Copy&quot; of the Solar Exaltation that leeched off of them for so long that they are now something of their own... and It's all part of the Plan for the Dragon....</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Infernal preview we know the Infernals are something of a plan to increase the power of the Yozi by having the exalt increase in power instead of the Yozi having to give it themselves. We also know Akumahood isn't what it used to be. What if a number of the Solars made the sort of pacts with the Yozi that Immaculates said they did and that the Yozi essence that tainted their Exaltations gestated while they were in the prison.<br /> <br /> So when the Deathlords broke the prison and created the Abyssals (or perhaps the Sids working already did that and the Deathlords just freed them) the Yozi essence got removed and became the core the Yozi used for their Exalted. This explains why Infernals are the smallest of the Solaroid faction and also why making more the old way wasn't a live option anymore.<br /> <br /> Edit: The fact that the Yozi were working with something incomplete, the demon incorporated as Coadjutor might have been necessary to make it work. The metaphysics are too ill defined to speculate with the new edition, but the Exaltation used to be conceived as something like a 3rd soul. Since the Yozi only had the hollow, exaltation shaped crust of essence that used to be around a Solar to work with the demon, which is a soul, could be acting to hold it together and to bind/ride/possess the human as the mechanism for bonding.<br /> <br /> This might tie in with the Yozi themes of not being able to make new things because of their mutilation. Infernals would be the most unstable or degradable of celestial like Exaltations, held together only with demonic patchwork and sustained by being grafted into the Yozi pantheons. It would have almost no mechanical effect, but might be a cool detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-25-2016, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T15:06:33-07:00","id":899438,"title":"","content":"Heck, if you're reworking setting assumptions, why bother with an actual, physical Jade Prison? Maybe the Sidereals just gamed destiny to make it impossible for Solar Exaltations to happen - the Unconquered Sun could override this (he can override anything), but he was all mad and turning his face from Creation and so forth, so mostly, he didn't (maybe once in a century, something roused his attention, hence the scant handful of Solars in that time).<br /> <br /> Then, something goes wrong (Demonic plots? Thulio? Terrible co-incidence?), the astrological laws of the cosmos shift, and some portion of sealed Solar power breaks through... into Hell. The Yozis are all over it, and since the Sun was delibreately ignoring that side of his nature, they rework this into their own Exalts.<br /> <br /> The moment one of these guys reaches Creation, the Unconquered Sun knows about it - and is overwhelmed with horror at what he has allowed. Creation has grown so corrupt, even the power of the Solars is a sign of its many evils! He swears to make the world right once more, and at that moment, a hundred Solars are reborn.<br /> <br /> ... or what have you. I see no reason why one of the greatest feats any of the Chosen ever accomplished ought to be a giant box which is eventually broken by a drill-squid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T15:33:46-07:00","id":899462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899438#post899438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, if you're reworking setting assumptions, why bother with an actual, physical Jade Prison? Maybe the Sidereals just gamed destiny to make it impossible for Solar Exaltations to happen - the Unconquered Sun could override this (he can override anything), but he was all mad and turning his face from Creation and so forth, so mostly, he didn't (maybe once in a century, something roused his attention, hence the scant handful of Solars in that time).<br /> <br /> Then, something goes wrong (Demonic plots? Thulio? Terrible co-incidence?), the astrological laws of the cosmos shift, and some portion of sealed Solar power breaks through... into Hell. The Yozis are all over it, and since the Sun was delibreately ignoring that side of his nature, they rework this into their own Exalts.<br /> <br /> The moment one of these guys reaches Creation, the Unconquered Sun knows about it - and is overwhelmed with horror at what he has allowed. Creation has grown so corrupt, even the power of the Solars is a sign of its many evils! He swears to make the world right once more, and at that moment, a hundred Solars are reborn.<br /> <br /> ... or what have you. I see no reason why one of the greatest feats any of the Chosen ever accomplished ought to be a giant box which is eventually broken by a drill-squid.</div> </div> </div> </div>The altering destiny thing has been my headcannon for years. That doesn't mean it can't also be a physical box. Or that the only way to break it is with the necromantic engine. The working that did it could have caused a great earthquake or agitated the exaltation/destiny threads/whatever was in it enough to break it from the inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-25-2016, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T15:46:58-07:00","id":899480,"title":"","content":"How did this thread get to discussing Infernals so quickly? When did Infernals develop their own version of Meerkat Steals the Spotlight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T15:50:26-07:00","id":899489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899480#post899480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did this thread get to discussing Infernals so quickly? When did Infernals develop their own version of Meerkat Steals the Spotlight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry... I just thought that it would be an interesting idea as an origin for all 3 &quot;Sun&quot; Based Exaltations...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T15:51:40-07:00","id":899490,"title":"","content":"Not mad, just making a joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:51:37-07:00","id":899546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899480#post899480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did this thread get to discussing Infernals so quickly? When did Infernals develop their own version of Meerkat Steals the Spotlight?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have always had it, its the main function of Malfeas' version of (Yozi) Commands Attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T19:27:37-07:00","id":899659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899462#post899462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The altering destiny thing has been my headcannon for years. That doesn't mean it can't also be a physical box. Or that the only way to break it is with the necromantic engine. The working that did it could have caused a great earthquake or agitated the exaltation/destiny threads/whatever was in it enough to break it from the inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>The possibility that such an Astrological working could require prayer slips, inked with crushed jade taken from the notched, chipped, and bloodied edges of ten thousand Dragon-blooded Daiklaives, placed at every cardinal point in Creation, would have a certain poetic irony to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 05-26-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:48:14-07:00","id":899989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899480#post899480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did this thread get to discussing Infernals so quickly? When did Infernals develop their own version of Meerkat Steals the Spotlight?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, how about them Lunars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T07:30:23-07:00","id":900012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899989#post899989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how about them Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly, do Lunars feel the same reaction towards these reimagined Abyssals as they do towards Solars?<br /> <br /> If their Lunar Exaltation was wedded to a Solar Exaltation in the First Age, does its Abyssal reflection also resonate as a wedded Exaltation?<br /> <br /> A Deathknight might thus find himself drawn to BOTH a particular Solar and a specific Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:21:23-07:00","id":900044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=900012#post900012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More importantly, do Lunars feel the same reaction towards these reimagined Abyssals as they do towards Solars?<br /> <br /> If their Lunar Exaltation was wedded to a Solar Exaltation in the First Age, does its Abyssal reflection also resonate as a wedded Exaltation?<br /> <br /> A Deathknight might thus find himself drawn to BOTH a particular Solar and a specific Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how you want to mirror the Abyssals and Solars, the Lunar might feel a strong antipathy towards the Abyssal mirror of her mate, just like moonlight is an enemy to the dark of night. It's not anyone's fault, but something about the Abyssal disquiets and upsets the Lunar, just like the undead upset natural animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:38:59-07:00","id":900071,"title":"","content":"I would say yes.<br /> <br /> If you're (1) playing up the Lunar Bond, and (2) introduce and Abyssal who has that connection to a Lunar character (or vice-versa), you certainly want that to be a thing. So, make it a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:15:45-07:00","id":900162,"title":"","content":"I recall someone saying that the Lunar Bond was one of the most powerful forces towards an Abyssal's redemption, because here's someone who knows what you could be, because they remember it, and even when everything else is dust they will never forget it. I don't remember if that was for a specific character, though. But I do love that sweet, sweet angst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:42:12-07:00","id":900178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=900162#post900162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall someone saying that the Lunar Bond was one of the most powerful forces towards an Abyssal's redemption</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means nothing if Abyssal Exaltations are a separate creation from Solar Exaltations. They cannot be redeemed into something they never were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:54:00-07:00","id":900183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Rakan Thulio did it. You can always blame Rakan Thulio for it. The Sidreals probably do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this one. I'd considered having Gold factioneers pull it off in the past but there are actual ingame reasons for having Rakan Thulio do it (unless he's completely with the Bronze faction on this one point). Having the Solars return would throw Heaven and Creation into chaos. Yu Shan would have to devote considerable time and energies elsewhere as a repurcussion of the Solars' return thus distracting Yu Shan and its agents in Crestion away from Thulio's designs. Also he may net some powerful allies with some Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":362,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","user":"Darkon","date":". 05-26-2016, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:39:42-07:00","id":900313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=899359#post899359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mirror charms didn't exactly go over well the last time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? What was the problem? I guess another way I could put it, in case I'm using the word &quot;mirror&quot; wrong in this context, is use the Solar Charmset, but change the aesthetics to an Abyssal theme or a shadow theme like I mentioned earlier. It's not the same I know, but it'll get the player by. Plus the player's description of the Charm's obvious effects can make it feel like a different Charm for the other players and ST.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:55:38-07:00","id":900329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=900313#post900313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? What was the problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>One problem with Mirrored Charms was that the writers took it as an opportunity to save on word-count by saying &quot;just go look at the mirrored Solar Charm in the corebook&quot;, which meant that you had to constantly check back and forth between two books and across two splats to see what ONE Charmset did.<br /> <br /> The other problem was that it felt to many people like the Abyssal Exalted had an overabundance of Mirrored Charms which meant that the Abyssal Exalted felt like they played TOO much like &quot;Solars painted black&quot;, especially since some of the mirrored effects were generally less useful because of a thematic bent towards pain and cruelty and destruction. Also, because Solars could use Holy effects to cause extra burn to Abyssals without Abyssals having a similar bite against Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:11:49-07:00","id":900341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=900178#post900178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which means nothing if Abyssal Exaltations are a separate creation from Solar Exaltations. They cannot be redeemed into something they never were.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Should never Need to be Redeemed, as they are not something that would be &quot;Evil&quot; Just the Lawgivers of another &quot;Plane&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T15:17:14-07:00","id":900406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=900313#post900313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? What was the problem? I guess another way I could put it, in case I'm using the word &quot;mirror&quot; wrong in this context, is <b>use the Solar Charmset, but change the aesthetics to an Abyssal theme or a shadow theme</b> like I mentioned earlier. It's not the same I know, but it'll get the player by. Plus the player's description of the Charm's obvious effects can make it feel like a different Charm for the other players and ST.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is the problem in a nutshell: that Abyssals were almost entirely dependent upon the existence of the Solar Charmset to function. In a perfect world, they could take out the Traits and Charms chapters, and replace the Sorcery section of the Martial Arts and Sorcery chapter, of Ex3, with Abyssal-focused crunch, and the book would be able to stand on its own. That wasn't exactly what we got last time around, which is why Mirror Charms get the side-eye from players like me. We really just want the Abyssals book to be its own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T15:40:14-07:00","id":900417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=900406#post900406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the problem in a nutshell: that Abyssals were almost entirely dependent upon the existence of the Solar Charmset to function. In a perfect world, they could take out the Traits and Charms chapters, and replace the Sorcery section of the Martial Arts and Sorcery chapter, of Ex3, with Abyssal-focused crunch, and the book would be able to stand on its own. That wasn't exactly what we got last time around, which is why Mirror Charms get the side-eye from players like me. We really just want the Abyssals book to be its own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also that problem of thematic divide. Abyssals didn't really have access to that many tricks where there wasn't a Solar version and what exclusive tricks they did have were fairly lackluster. The Abyssals preview, other than triggering Rapegate, was a piece that provided a lot of hope by showing an Abyssal Charm set with its own way of doing things, like slamming enemies into conjured iron maidens and animating their corpses as your own iron knights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T15:57:20-07:00","id":900425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=900329#post900329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, because Solars could use Holy effects to cause extra burn to Abyssals without Abyssals having a similar bite against Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that a feature rather than a bug? Much like how vampires have to &quot;suffer&quot; the blood hunger Abyssals had to deal with the fact that they were unnatural in some sense as far as the bright shiny Creation was concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:07:12-07:00","id":900430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=900425#post900425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that a feature rather than a bug? Much like how vampires have to &quot;suffer&quot; the blood hunger Abyssals had to deal with the fact that they were unnatural in some sense as far as the bright shiny Creation was concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was presented as a feature. Many players saw it as a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:08:34-07:00","id":900432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898955-alternate-origin-for-abyssal-exaltations?p=900425#post900425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that a feature rather than a bug? Much like how vampires have to &quot;suffer&quot; the blood hunger Abyssals had to deal with the fact that they were unnatural in some sense as far as the bright shiny Creation was concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except there aren't &quot;Anti-Vampires&quot; that have all of the same powers but don't drink blood or burn under the sun, which is what Solars would be.<br /> <br /> Vampires instead generally have to worry about werewolves, who suffer a fatal allergy to silver, or mages, who are just as squishy as any normal human if you catch them by surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T23:46:30-07:00","id":900734,"title":"","content":"I think that Abyssal &quot;unnaturalness&quot; is cool as a theme, but it's more fun to explore it with their charm thematics rather than making it a pure disadvantage.<br /> <br /> eg. I'd assume Abyssals tend to have more obviously unnatural charms than Solars do, which is both an advantage (it means you can get charms that do some weirder stuff) and a disadvantage (it means you have fewer options for passing as mortal.) The fact that many Abyssal charms tend to look terrifying, horrifying, or, even on their best days, ominous and intimidating is also a decent way to represent it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T00:46:32-07:00","id":900759,"title":"","content":"If your Going by the Original Post for this then i'd say that the Charms of an Abyssal are no more unnatural then Those of the Dead... The Cycle shouldn't have allowed this to happen but it has. Because it has the Charms are perfectly Natural.... In the Underworld. In Creation they Should have the Unnatural Tag (If that is still a Thing) I'd suggest that the Solar charms ALSO Gain that Tag while in the Underworld... They Aren't from the same origin as the Dead and henceforth aren't Natural to that Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T10:57:21-07:00","id":905055,"title":"","content":"What if the Abyssals were more directly a product of the Usurpation? The Underworld was created by the pseudo-death of the Primordials, the Usurpation was the single biggest instance of death and destruction since that time, what if the near-overnight death of so many Solar exalted had far more of a straining effect on reality than just 'lotsa Solar ghosts now roaming the underworld being ideal candidates to become Deathlords', and so many severed Exaltations flying around at once, with powerful ghosts all dropping into the Underworld, started getting tangled with each other and picking up threads of Underworld-aspected essence?<br /> <br /> The Bronze Faction had their plan and all, Chejop was set to catch nearly all the Solar Essences in the Jade Prison (physical, a cut off destiny-loop, or whatever you want it to actually be) and keep them there indefinitely, but since Sidereals can't predict anything having to do with the Underworld, they didn't see how such a massive Solar die-off could affect that until it was already happening. Some attentive Sidereal noticed, and relayed to Chejop, &quot;Hey, something's not quite right, the sudden death of all these Solars is doing something to their exaltations&quot;, and Chejop made the conscious choice to say, &quot;Stick to the plan&quot;. Sidereal hubris prevented him from seeing that a Jade Prison specifically calibrated to contain Solar exaltations might run into problems containing exaltations that had been warped and tangled with threads of the underworld during the massacre, which would introduce weaknesses in the prison that might slowly grow over time, and get to the point where some knowledgeable, powerful being with a reason could break open the prison through those weaknesses.<br /> <br /> It gives an added layer of emotion, as on some level Chejop has to realize he's the one ultimately responsible for the creation of the Abyssals. And in my personal headcanon, I like to think it was the Scarlet Empress who kicked open the prison, physical or not. For whatever reason, she was tired of Sidereal meddling, she knew of the prison through her close association with Chejop, and since she didn't suffer the Great Curse of hubris, she saw the weaknesses in the prison that he blinded himself to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11640-djinnkitty83","name":"Djinnkitty83","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}